It's true, though.  "Bless you" and "Gesundheit" are both appropriate. 
English (or maybe just American English) has a tendency to, well not so much 
'borrow' words, as much as chase down other languages, knock them down in 
dark alleys and rifle through their lexicons for words it likes. 
Figuratively speaking, of course ;-)  American English these days has a 
strong Germanic strain running through it, due to German immigrants from a 
couple centuries ago.  English is such a compound language anyway, with 
Latin and Greek roots as well, it doesn't strain speakers much more to add 
words with flavor.

That's why one mouse plus one mouse: two mice
One louse plus another: two lice
One house plus another: two *houses*

Makes spelling and pluralization much more... interesting.  Box: Boxes, Fox: 
Foxes, Ox: Oxen, Vax: Vaxen ;)

C'est la vie :)

